 "text": "Hi, how are things with you? It' understandable to feel guilty about taking breaks when you' at home, though. At home, it' easy to keep working instead of taking a break. One way to combat that is to schedule your breaks. Turn off notifications for them, and see them as part of your work day. Something quick and mental, like a deep breath break, or few mindful movements. A short cup of tea, or quick stretch, if you have space. Definitely not. Phones are a huge time sink during breaks, and make you want keep going. The tea is great, and taking a quick window break in middle helps prevent it from building up.",
